# Reflaxe.Elixir (haxelib/lix extra params)
#
# This file is consumed automatically when a project uses:
#   -lib reflaxe.elixir
#
# IMPORTANT: Keep this file *cwd-agnostic*.
# - Do not add relative classpaths like `-cp src` or `-cp std` here: those would
#   be resolved relative to the *consumer project*, not this library.
#
# Bootstraps the target after Haxe has resolved the library classpath.
# Source-checkout std override paths must be supplied before typing via
# haxe_libraries/reflaxe.elixir.hxml or direct repo-local hxml files; macros in
# this file run too late to guarantee ownership of every upstream-colliding std
# module. Reflaxe package builds flatten std/elixir/_std into packaged
# .cross.hx files, so installed consumers only need `-lib reflaxe.elixir`.
--macro reflaxe.elixir.CompilerBootstrap.Start()
--macro reflaxe.elixir.CompilerInit.Start()

# Preserve functional shapes for Elixir output
-D loop_unroll_max_cost=0
